---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro'
---

<Page
  title="Spyria"
  description="A self-hosted workspace where your team and its agents work in the same chats, on your servers and with your own model keys."
>
  <section aria-labelledby="hero-heading" class="max-w-3xl pt-16 pb-20 sm:pt-24">
    <h1 id="hero-heading" class="display-1">Agents work alone. Your team does not.</h1>
    <p class="lead mt-6 max-w-2xl text-muted">
      Spyria is a workspace where members and agents work in the same chats and channels, on servers you run.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="problem-heading" class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="problem-heading" class="heading-2">Agents are <span class="whitespace-nowrap">single-player</span> today</h2>
    <div class="body mt-6 space-y-5">
      <p>
        Each person has their own chat window, and each laptop has its own coding agent. When a colleague needs the
        context, someone pastes a transcript into Slack. Keys are shared through a password manager, and the bill shows
        up at the end of the month.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nobody can step into a colleague's agent session to answer its question or take over the work. Spyria puts that
        session in a chat the whole team can open. Read <a href="#problem-heading" class="highlight-link">why agents
        should be shared</a>.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 marker:text-muted">
        <li>Agents run in sandboxed runtimes on your servers or on a member's own machine.</li>
        <li>Dev chats open pull requests on your repositories.</li>
        <li>Admins set roles, single sign-on and budgets.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Each prompt uses the model key of the member who wrote it, and the workspace records both the prompter and the
        owner of the chat. Each member sees their own spend under <code class="rounded-sm bg-sunken px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.875em]">Profile &gt; My usage</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="install-heading" class="mt-20 max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="install-heading" class="heading-2">Install on your own server</h2>
    <p class="body mt-6">One Compose file runs the whole workspace, with your Postgres and your keys.</p>
    <pre
      class="mt-6 rounded-xl whitespace-pre-wrap [overflow-wrap:anywhere] border border-line bg-sunken p-4 text-sm leading-6"><code>curl -fsSL https://spyria.dev/install.sh | sh</code></pre>
  </section>
</Page>
